  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1258 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nOutflow from the Thu night activity is forecast to stall across\nthe CEN or SRN Panhandles on Friday. Tons of high H7 Theta-e\nassociated with the monsoon plume are forecast to combine with\nincreased low level moisture from the Gulf to provide anomalously\nhigh moisture and model soundings show SBCAPE improving to\n1500-2000 j/kg despite ridiculously warm H5 temps near -2 deg C. \nIn addition, there is actually still some wind shear to work with \nas NAM and GFS both indicate bulk effective shear of 20 to 40 \nalong the boundary mainly due to directional shear. One wonders \nif we will see any supercell structure similar to July 4th event, \nbut CAPE is not as high as that even and mid level temps are much \nwarmer. If we do, right mover motion is WSW similar to July 4th. \nAgain, SVR convective parameters suggest mainly a wind threat with\nthese and suspect SPC will end up including a marginal for Friday\neventually. High moisture suggests a heavy rainfall threat as \npotential for very high rates may exist and if everything comes \ntogether localized areas could see 2 inches in less than an hour.\nOnion soundings in the evening suggest a threat for heat bursts \nas well. Main caveats for Friday will be exact boundary location \nand timing of the ridge riding S/WV. Heat advisory conditions seem\nunlikely given this set-up unless the boundary stalls further \nnorth. Some models develop convection very early across the area \nwhich would likely keep much of the area well below 100 even. Gut \nfeeling is the storms will be forming by early afternoon. NBM \ntrended cooler and left it as is for now, but it could still be \ntoo hot near the boundary location.\n\nAs the ridge builds just north of the area on Saturday once \nagain, the southern Panhandles remain below a weakness that will\nbe drifting west under the ridge. There is enough lingering moisture\nappears to suggests at least isolated storms mainly across the \nsouthern TX Panhandle. This would likely preclude temps much above\n100 once again. The high center will build more over the area \nagain Sunday and into early next week and as it does, temperatures\nwill soar above 100 once again as moisture decreases. Monday \ncurrently has the highest probabilities for seeing temperatures \ngreater than 104 at anywhere from 20 percent in the far west to \n70+ percent in the PDC and Canadian River Valley from Miami to \nBoys Ranch.",
